# Project‑Based Permissions (RBAC)

The Kanban app enforces fine‑grained, per‑project access control through a
**role‑based access control (RBAC)** system. Permissions are evaluated on the
server for **every protected endpoint** – the client UI may hide or show
controls, but the final decision is always made by the backend.

---

## 1️⃣ Roles

| Role   | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| **owner**   | The user who created the project. Implicitly has every permission, even if the `project_members` table does not contain a row for them. |
| **admin**   | Can manage members, boards, tags, and all tasks. |
| **manager**| Can create/ edit/ delete tasks, assign tasks, and add boards. |
| **member**  | Limited to actions explicitly allowed by the project’s **settings** (see below). |

Roles are stored in `project_members.role` (type `varchar`).  
When a user is the **owner**, the system treats them as `owner` regardless of the
`project_members` entry.

---

## 2️⃣ Permission Context Helpers

Two utility functions expose a **permission context** that downstream services
and controllers use:

| Helper | Purpose | Returned shape (relevant fields) |
|--------|---------|----------------------------------|
| `getProjectPermissionContext({ projectId, requesterId })` | Loads the project, its owner, the requester’s role, and the project‑wide settings. | `projectId`, `ownerId`, `requesterId`, `requesterRole`, `isOwner`, `isAdmin`, `isManager`, `isMember`, `settings` (see below). |
| `getTaskPermissionContext({ taskId, requesterId })` | Same as above, but also loads the task’s creator, its project, and whether the requester is an assignee. | All fields from the project context **plus** `taskId`, `isCreator`, `isAssignee`. |

Both helpers are defined in **`server/utils/projectPermissions.js`** and
throw a **403** (`PROJECT_FORBIDDEN`) if the requester is not a member of the
project.

---

## 3️⃣ Project Settings (Feature Flags)

Each project has a row in **`project_settings`** that stores Boolean flags
controlling what members are allowed to do. The flags are read via the
permission helpers and are exposed to the client through the project API
responses.

| Flag | Default | What it controls |
|------|---------|-------------------|
| `allow_member_create_task` | `true` | Member may create new tasks. |
| `allow_member_take_task` | `true` | Member may **self‑assign** or assign to others (if `allow_assign_task_to_member` is also true). |
| `allow_member_edit_task` | `true` | Member may edit task details. |
| `allow_member_delete_task` | `true` | Member may delete tasks. |
| `allow_member_add_board` | `true` | Member may create new boards. |
| `allow_member_add_member` | `true` | Member may invite other users to the project. |
| `allow_member_review` | `false` | Member may mark a task as “reviewed”. |
| `allow_assign_task_to_member` | `false` | Member may assign a task to **another** member (owner/admin can always assign). |
| `allow_admin_add_member` | `true` | Admin can add members. |
| `allow_admin_remove_member` | `true` | Admin can remove members. |
| `allow_admin_add_board` | `true` | Admin can add boards. |
| `allow_admin_manage_tasks` | `true` | Admin can edit/delete any task regardless of member flags. |
| `allow_admin_create_tag` | `true` | Admin can create tags. |
| `allow_member_create_tag` | `false` | Member may create tags (if enabled). |

> **Tip:** When adding a new feature that depends on a permission, create a
> corresponding column in `project_settings` and expose it through the
> `settings` object returned by the helpers.

